    "title": "Interlanguage and Mathematical Translation Methodology Sidecar (v0.4 Consolidated Interface Refresh)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21300808",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-10",
    "description": "<p>This record preserves the interlanguage and constructed-language methodology sidecar for the Modern LaTeX Manuscripts project: Interslavic and Slavic translation governance, weighted automata and term-weight ledgers, multilingual source-body support packages, and Claude/ChatGPT/Fable provenance and executable methodology.</p><p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_Interlanguage_Methodology_Current_20260710.pdf</code>. File <code>11_Interlanguage_Claude_Fable_v04_Consolidated_Methodology_20260710.zip</code> contains the complete current methodology workspace: ordered v0.4 framework, consolidated interface HTML/JSON, global connective table, column crosschecks, branch-weighting specifications, source-use and adverse ledgers, context-review queues, scripts, corpus maps, and provenance notes.</p><p><strong>Current result:</strong> the global connective analysis finds that 10 of 15 connective rows lack even a Slavic-internal pan-root and none has a secure cross-family global attractor. The honest design space therefore includes explicit gloss blocks, symbolic forms, or designed bridge forms rather than a false claim of universal inherited vocabulary.</p><p><strong>Status caveat:</strong> this is methodology, source-body routing, provenance, and corpus infrastructure. It is not native-speaker approval, accepted terminology, a finished interlanguage, mathematical source-fidelity certification, reader completion, or proof that any language branch is complete. Generated translation material remains distinct from independent source bodies and reviewer evidence.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, additional source bodies, better weighting heuristics, and cleaned language-branch packages can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
